  "body": "Found while fixing #1529 (the Top/Bottom of Model heights, which now read only the parts through `setup_align::part_aabb_in`).\n\nWhat happens (code reading, upstream/main 41cd9c2): the GUI's stock fit (`crates/ui/src/state.rs` ~3059, 3071, 3089: box fit, cylinder radius via `solid_radius_about_in`, and the second fit path) and the stock info strip (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/stock_info.rs:13`) read `setup_align::solid_aabb_in`, which walks every `model::model_entities` entry - fixtures included. With a vise, soft jaw, plate or tagged fixture placed, \"fit stock to models\" sizes the stock around the workholding, not the part.\n\nExpected: fitting the stock to the models measures the parts only (the same set #1529's `part_aabb_in` uses; the cylinder fit needs a part-only radius twin of `solid_radius_about_in`). Collision checks keep seeing the fixtures.\n\nNot exercised: no test drives this yet; this is from reading the callers. The MCP `set_stock` fit path should be checked for the same set.\n\nDone means: with a vise placed, the GUI box and cylinder fits and the stock info read the part's bounds; a pinning test per fit kind with and without a vise gives the same stock.\n\nRelated: #1529, #1094.\n",
